sequenceDiagram
  accTitle: Product X uncertainty and resource control sequence
  accDescr: A Product X incident first receives incomplete evidence. A proposal carries a linked uncertainty estimate, the scheduler reserves a read-only diagnostic slot, and policy authorizes that exact read. New telemetry revises the estimate. The monitor preempts low-priority summarization at a safe boundary. A production write is denied because the principal did not delegate that authority. The investigation stops with either a verified result or an explicit insufficient-evidence outcome.
  participant O as Operator
  participant R as Runtime
  participant U as Uncertainty registry
  participant S as Scheduler
  participant G as Authorization gate
  participant T as Tool service
  participant M as Monitor
  O->>R: Open incident investigation
  R->>U: Attach evidence-linked estimate to diagnostic proposal
  U-->>R: Estimate revision 1 and calibration context
  R->>S: Request typed read-only resource vector
  S-->>R: Reserve diagnostic slot within deadline
  R->>G: Request authorization for exact health query
  G-->>R: Authorized within read-only scope
  R->>T: Execute health query
  T-->>R: Partial result and new telemetry
  R->>U: Create linked estimate revision 2
  R->>M: Publish run state and active resource use
  M->>S: Request safe preemption of low-priority work
  S-->>M: Safe-boundary checkpoint confirmed
  R->>G: Propose production restart
  G-->>R: Denied because restart authority was not delegated
  R->>U: Evaluate stopping decision using latest estimate
  U-->>R: Risk and evidence status
  R-->>O: Report verified diagnosis or explicit uncertainty
